# Where the whole program is open, unknown JavaScript names the global object, and from there every built-in. Native code calls each of them once for the program, in a statement of its own with unknown operands,
# and a built-in that such a call runs in turn is one more statement: the work grows with the number of built-ins, not with the ways to reach one from another.
# OPTIONS: admit=RuntimeCode
# RUN: flow-solve sinks
# RUN(STATEMENTS): flow-links statements
# STATISTIC: FlowWorklistSteps <= 60000

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    Return
}
# CHECK: nativeCode {unknown, GlobalThis,
# CHECK: unknownJavaScript {unknown, GlobalThis,
# STATEMENTS: statement i0 - ArrayPrototypeJoin Call Host Repeatedly
# STATEMENTS-NOT: statement i0 - ArrayPrototypeJoin Call Host Repeatedly
